%% Theme 05 — Supporting sequence: correction races a booking (ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md §10.6)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User via harness
    participant K as Session kernel
    participant H as Harness tools

    U->>K: "Yes, book the 7:05" + end of turn
    Note over K: operation (g1, book_flight) is FREE · commit barrier holds
    K-)H: tool call c3 book_flight · passengers 1
    Note over K: operation LOCKED · attempt c3 PENDING
    U->>K: "wait, two of us"
    Note over K: passengers → 2 (last writer wins) · c3 SUPERSEDED
    K-)H: advisory cancel c3
    U->>K: end of turn
    Note over K: desired: book with passengers 2<br/>operation is LOCKED → NO new create is dispatched
    K->>U: "I'd already started booking for one, checking whether it went through"

    alt the harness completes c3 anyway
        H--)K: result c3 OK · booking B1
        Note over K: operation COMMITTED with passengers 1 ≠ desired 2
        K-)H: tool call c4 modify_booking(B1, passengers 2) · NEW operation, only if the manifest offers it
        K->>U: "It went through for one, updating it to two"
    else the harness honours the cancel or reports not executed
        H--)K: result c3 cancelled / error, not executed
        Note over K: attempt FAILED_CLEAN → operation FREE
        K-)H: tool call c5 book_flight · passengers 2
    else no result before the timeout
        Note over K: attempt UNKNOWN → operation stays LOCKED
        K->>U: "I can't confirm the first booking. Check it before I book again?"
    end
